{
  "comment": [
    "Shared boundary vectors for the C2-R3 ruled timestamp rule",
    "(docs/completed/CONSENSUS_C2_R3_TIMESTAMPS.md §4.3, ratified 2026-09-01):",
    "a candidate timestamp T is consensus-valid iff T <= local_clock + 540",
    "(FTL) and T > M (MTP), where M is element index 5 (0-based) of the",
    "sorted window of the 11 timestamps immediately preceding the candidate,",
    "the window right-padded with the genesis timestamp when fewer than 11",
    "predecessors exist. Callers with deeper history select the NEWEST 11",
    "before calling (C2-R3-Q1 sub-a); a wider window is a caller bug and is",
    "refused, never silently medianed.",
    "",
    "Consumers: C++ tests/unit_tests/mtp_boundary.cpp (production rule",
    "function shekyl_check_timestamp_rule — all sections) and Rust",
    "rust/shekyl-difficulty/tests/mtp_boundary_vectors.rs (production",
    "predicates is_above_mtp / is_timestamp_below_ftl — predicate_cases and",
    "ftl_cases; assembly_cases gain their Rust consumer when the rewrite",
    "grows window assembly at the C3 cutover). Two implementations of one",
    "rule that do not share vectors drift silently.",
    "",
    "Vectors are pinned per rule 30: a change here is a consensus change and",
    "requires review + a CHANGELOG entry."
  ],
  "constants": {
    "mtp_window": 11,
    "median_index_of_sorted_window": 5,
    "ftl_seconds": 540
  },
